# Build context trimming. The repo carries a lot of weight that has no business
# in a runtime image, and on a Pi every avoided megabyte is real time.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.flake8
.vscode
.idea
.claude

# Built by the venv-builder stage at the same absolute path; copying a host
# venv in would shadow it with one built for the wrong arch and python.
birdnet/

# x86_64 gotty is 13MB of dead weight in an arm64 image. scripts/gotty
# dispatches on uname -m and only ever reaches the aarch64 binary here.
scripts/gotty-x86_64

# The optional e-ink wall display. Separate device, separate installer
# (frame/install.sh), no role in the server container.
frame/

# Docs and screenshots. Nothing served at runtime reads a markdown file; the
# double-star is needed because a bare *.md would only match the context root.
docs/
**/*.md
!version.md

# Test suite and CI fixtures.
tests/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The illustration generation pipeline: a developer tool that calls the Gemini
# and eBird APIs to regenerate avian/assets. The generated assets ship; the
# generator does not.
avian/scripts/
avian/assets/references/
avian/assets/_legacy/

# Local runtime state from a bare-metal install that happens to share the
# directory. These are seeded onto volumes by avian-container-init.
birdnet.conf
BirdDB.txt
IdentifiedSoFar.txt*
apprise.txt
body.txt
firstrun.ini
HUMAN.txt
*_species_list.txt
scripts/*.db
installation-*.txt

# Docker build inputs are COPYed explicitly by path, so the directory itself
# does not need to land in the image root.
docker-compose.yml
.env
.env.example
